<title>UK: Reuters 1st ex-UK Americas/Africa/Nordic air cargo.</title>
<headline>Reuters 1st ex-UK Americas/Africa/Nordic air cargo.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the current average ex-UK to the United States, Latin America Africa and Scandinavia per kg for a 100 kg shipment, with a volume-to-weight ratio of six-to-one.</p>
<p>	    Feb 13	     Jan 24</p>
<p>		  UNITED STATES</p>
<p>     LON-JFK   0.65		 0.64</p>
<p>     LON-LAX   0.80		 0.75</p>
<p>     LON-CHI   0.76		 0.76</p>
<p>		  LATIN AMERICA</p>
<p>     LON-SAO   2.10		 2.06</p>
<p>     LON-BUE   2.19		 2.19</p>
<p>		  AFRICA</p>
<p>     LON-JNB   1.65		 1.72</p>
<p>     LON-NBO   0.95		 -</p>
<p>		  SCANDINAVIA</p>
<p>     LON-STO   0.75		 0.75</p>
<p>     LON-CPH   0.70		 0.70</p>
<p>*The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuters journalists on a confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents at the three main London airports.</p>
<p>*All prices are quoted in sterling.</p>
<p>*The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices and are indicative of current market activity.</p>
</text>
